			ἡ</span>. a house <i>but half complete</i>, i.e. childless,
				<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.701
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					7.3.3
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>DMort.</u>
				19.1
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀλύμπιον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dicaearch.
					1.1
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ. θάλαμος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					7.627
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Diod.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ. νίκη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					2.42
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φωναί</span>”
